      "side": 1,
      "message": "Marking `NOTREACHED()` as `[[noreturn]]` means it must not return, and calling `std::abort()` ensures this. However, this causes `NOTREACHED()` to become **fatal in release builds**, whereas previously `DCHECK(false)` was ignored or compiled away when `DCHECK_IS_ON()` was false.\n\nIf making it fatal everywhere is intended (e.g. to prevent undefined behavior when falling off the end of a function), consider using `IMMEDIATE_CRASH()` instead of `std::abort()`. `IMMEDIATE_CRASH()` is defined earlier in this file and is designed to play well with crash reporters and preserve good crash signatures.\n\n```suggestion\n    IMMEDIATE_CRASH();\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 810,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 810,
        "endChar": 0
      },
