      "writtenOn": "2026-08-20T04:54:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: Because `.stream()` returns `std::ostream\u0026`, using this macro as a standalone statement (e.g. `NOTREACHED();` or `NOTREACHED() \u003c\u003c \\\"message\\\";`) will evaluate to `std::ostream\u0026` and likely trigger an `unused-value` compiler warning.\n\nYou can wrap the expression with `LogMessageVoidify` (similar to how `LAZY_STREAM` and other logging macros work) so it evaluates to `void` and suppresses the warning:\n\n```suggestion\n#define NOTREACHED() \\\n  ::logging::LogMessageVoidify() \u0026 \\\n  ::logging::NotReachedLogMessage(__FILE__, __LINE__).stream()\n```",
